{"name":"Blue Cypress","hex":"#cbdbd7","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"cypress","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evergreen coniferous tree with flattened shoots bearing small scale-like leaves, whose dark foliage is sometimes associated with mourning, in family Cupressaceae, especially the genera Cupressus and Chamaecyparis."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of Cyprus (“type of fabric”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cypress"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hesperocyparis guadalupensis","blocks":[{"text":"Hesperocyparis guadalupensis, the Guadalupe cypress, is a species of conifer in the cypress family, Cupressaceae, endemic to Guadalupe Island in the Pacific Ocean off the western coast of Mexico's Baja Peninsula. It is a medium-sized tree with fine green to blue-green foliage. In its native habitat it depends on water from the fogs that envelop high ground in the northern half of the island."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Cupressus_guadalupensis.JPG/330px-Cupressus_guadalupensis.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hesperocyparis_guadalupensis"},{"title":"Cypress","blocks":[{"text":"Cypress is a common name for species in several genera in the family Cupressaceae. They grow in temperate climates and subtropical regions of Asia, Europe, and North America."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cypress"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Cupressus_guadalupensis_trunk.JPG/500px-Cupressus_guadalupensis_trunk.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Cupressus_guadalupensis_trunk.JPG/1280px-Cupressus_guadalupensis_trunk.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Cupressus_guadalupensis_trunk.JPG/500px-Cupressus_guadalupensis_trunk.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hesperocyparis guadalupensis bark - Golden Gate Park, San Francisco, California","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACupressus_guadalupensis_trunk.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Hesperocyparis_guadalupensis_-_Thibaud_Aronson_01.jpg/500px-Hesperocyparis_guadalupensis_-_Thibaud_Aronson_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Hesperocyparis_guadalupensis_-_Thibaud_Aronson_01.jpg/1280px-Hesperocyparis_guadalupensis_-_Thibaud_Aronson_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Hesperocyparis_guadalupensis_-_Thibaud_Aronson_01.jpg/500px-Hesperocyparis_guadalupensis_-_Thibaud_Aronson_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hesperocyparis guadalupensis showing regeneration after the removal of goats from Guadalupe Island. Photographed in 2015","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHesperocyparis_guadalupensis_-_Thibaud_Aronson_01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Actinostrobos_arenarius_fruits_murchison.JPG/330px-Actinostrobos_arenarius_fruits_murchison.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Actinostrobos_arenarius_fruits_murchison.JPG/960px-Actinostrobos_arenarius_fruits_murchison.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Actinostrobos_arenarius_fruits_murchison.JPG/330px-Actinostrobos_arenarius_fruits_murchison.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AActinostrobos_arenarius_fruits_murchison.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Austrocedrus_chilensis_por_pabloendemico_-_001.jpg/250px-Austrocedrus_chilensis_por_pabloendemico_-_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Austrocedrus_chilensis_por_pabloendemico_-_001.jpg/330px-Austrocedrus_chilensis_por_pabloendemico_-_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6